DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  return  the  hyperbolic cosine of _x, which is defined
       mathematically as:

           cosh(x) = (exp(x) + exp(-x)) / 2

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the hyperbolic cosine of _x.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is +0 or -0, 1 is returned.

       If _x is positive infinity or negative infinity,  positive  infinity  is
       returned.

       If the result overflows, a range error occurs, and the functions return
       +HHUUGGEE__VVAALL, +HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF, or +HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively.

